  "summary": "Full assessment of all 143 Japanese/Vietnamese passages in twenty sections and both titles. The retainer’s account of the lord of Horikawa, the painter Yoshihide, his daughter and the monkey, the commission of the hell screen, the burning carriage and Yoshihide’s death is complete, with the narrator’s deference and evasions intact and the source’s own inconsistencies preserved. The separate-context pass scored 8.85 with no major findings and fourteen minor ones, including the title; the substantive items were revised. Fidelity, voice, imagery and mechanics are 9.0, naturalness 8.5. Unrounded weighted score 8.925 meets the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
  "title_review": {
    "source_title": "地獄變",
    "target_title": "Địa ngục biến",
    "rationale": "Địa ngục biến is the established Sino-Vietnamese title and the term the body uses for the screen; 變 names a picture of the transformations of hell, which a descriptive title would lose."
  }
